    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13264" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēpugnātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		depugno, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a violent fighting, eager contest</i> (ante- and
			postclass.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.,
			Cato ap. <i><span class="en">Non. 204, 32</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Veg. Mil. 3, 30</span></i> et
			saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Of debate: forensium
			certaminum depugnationes, Firm. Math. 4
			praef.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A defacing</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">humani oris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Spect. 18</span></i>
			.</div>
